  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion provides any benefit over a unimodal baseline. Without a reference floor, no multimodal result can be interpreted. config_004 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) establishes a clean, standard RNA-only baseline: it uses a well-understood linear encoder (pca_n2000), the multiprofile setting that matches the majority of multimodal candidates, and simple avgpool aggregation. This makes it directly comparable to multimodal extensions such as config_015 or config_033 (which add resnet50 + a fusion mechanism), isolating the effect of adding the image modality. Choosing RNA-only over image-only is preferred because the RNA encoder dimension (pca vs scgpt vs scvi) is the more variable and less certain axis in this design space, and RNA is the primary biological signal in cellular profiling. This single experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty—whether the multimodal premise is even supported—before spending budget exploring the multimodal configuration space."
}

